-- THIS FILE DOES NOT WORK YET, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE OF ITEM `~mgqwb`.
--
-- What it is supposed to do: you import it, elaboration runs by itself, reaches
-- the hole below, and hands you the unfinished proof to finish.
--
--   cabal run thena
--   :consult examples/demo/Demo08Pausing.thena.rules
--   import examples.demo.pending.Demo07Holes
--
-- WHAT YOU GET INSTEAD. The rule in `Demo08Pausing` fires — its message
-- prints, so elaboration really did reach the hole and really did yield — and
-- then the suspension is thrown away when the load returns:
--
--   a placeholder: fill it and `yield` to carry on
--   (yield to hand control back)
--   :where   -->  let ? goal : Type₀      (a fresh, empty scratch goal)
--   yield    -->  nothing has yielded
--   :infer zeroIsValue
--            -->  not in scope: zeroIsValue
--
-- A module elaborates in an ISOLATED session, and nothing carries a standing
-- machine back out of it. **Everything else already works**: typed at the
-- prompt, the identical declaration suspends on this very goal and finishes —
--
--   declare zeroIsValue : value`0 value` ; zeroIsValue = _
--   a placeholder: fill it and `yield` to carry on
--   :where   -->  focus  let ? goal : value`0 value`
--                 path   root ▸ zeroIsValue
--                 type   value`0 value`
--   try-core core`V-num zero NV-zero`
--   solve
--   yield
--   :infer zeroIsValue   -->  zeroIsValue : value`0 value`
--
-- WITHOUT `Demo08Pausing` CONSULTED the file gets the plain refusal instead,
-- because the shipped base's two clauses for a hole have empty bodies and the
-- declaration is then finished with the hole still open:
--
--   stuck: not finished: the hole goal is still open, so there is no term yet
--
-- The file is kept here, ready, so that `~mgqwb` has something to be tested
-- against the day it lands.

